Test Materials (prototype/tests/*.musicxml)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MusicXML files under prototype/tests/ are derived from the BWV 66
(Johann Sebastian Bach, 1685–1750) chorale. Bach's compositions are in the
public domain as the copyright protection period has expired.

The specific MusicXML encodings in this repository were generated or derived
using music21. Because music21 itself is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause
License (see above), any encoding produced by or distributed with music21 may
carry music21's license obligations.

Action required before redistribution:
  - Confirm whether the specific .musicxml files in prototype/tests/ are
    directly sourced from the music21 corpus or were independently generated.
  - If music21 corpus files are included, ensure the music21 BSD 3-Clause
    attribution notice is preserved.
  - If independently generated from public-domain source material, confirm
    that no proprietary encoding or notation software imposes additional
    restrictions.

This confirmation has not been completed as of the initial repository setup.
It is tracked as an open issue (05_ARCHITECTURE_DESIGN.md TBD-005 /
06_OPERATION_AND_HANDOFF.md TBD-005).
